{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q391679","formula":"CHNO","hill":"CHNO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":1.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Cyanic acid","ru":"Циановая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Isocyanic acid is a chemical compound with the structural formula HNCO, which is often written as H−N=C=O. It is a colourless, volatile and poisonous gas, condensing at 23.5 °C. It is the predominant tautomer and an isomer of cyanic acid (aka. cyanol) (H−O−C≡N), and the monomer of cyanuric acid. The derived anion of isocyanic acid is the same as the derived anion of cyanic acid, and that anion is [N=C=O]−, which is called cyanate.","ru":"Изоциа́новая кислота́ — бесцветная жидкость с резким запахом, схожим с запахом уксусной кислоты, является стабильной таутомерной формой циановой кислоты HOCN. В высоких концентрациях — токсична. Соли циановой кислоты впервые описаны Вёлером в 1824 г., сама циановая кислота получена Либихом и Вёлером в 1830 г.. Является изомером фульминовой (парациановой) кислоты (H-C≡N→O)."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":540,"mass":43.025,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(#N)O","inchikey":"XLJMAIOERFSOGZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"cyanic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"540","atoms":4,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.272,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.216,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.056,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.611,"y":0.824,"z":0.388,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,2,1],[0,3,1],[1,2,3]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q391679","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyanic_acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A6%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0